   WORKFLOW PIPELINE FOR EACH SIMULATION: preprocess -> simsetup -> hpcjob -> analysis -> reporter

   Tool sections below match the workflow agents in --subtask. Per-simulation tools are for: preprocess, simsetup, hpcjob, analysis, reporter. Cross-simulation tools run once at the project base after all per-sim runs.

   PER-SIMULATION TOOLS (one section per workflow agent; excludes cross-sim tools):
   **PREPROCESS AGENT:**
   Role: PDB cleanup, validation, hydrogen addition
     • acquire_protein_structure(user_request, output_dir, source): Download and prepare a protein structure when no PDB file is provided.
     • add_hydrogens(pdb_file, output_file, method, ph, molecule_type): Add missing hydrogen atoms to PDB file with appropriate tool based on molecule type.
     • align_model_to_experimental(target_pdb, donor_pdb, output_file, target_chain, donor_chain): Superpose donor structure onto experimental target and write aligned donor PDB.
     • analyze_pdb(pdb_file): Analyze PDB/GRO file structure and composition using MDAnalysis.
     • detect_missing_structure_elements(target_pdb, donor_pdb, target_chain, donor_chain, check_atoms): Align experimental and model structures by sequence and report gaps.
     • download_structure(uniprot_id, output_file, source, source_order): Download a protein structure for a UniProt accession from AlphaFold DB,
     • extract_domain(pdb_file, start_resid, end_resid, output_file, chain_id, protein_name, domain_name): Extract a protein domain by UniProt/PDB residue numbering.
     • lookup_domain_range_tool(uniprot_id, domain_label, source_order): Look up UniProt residue boundaries for a protein domain.
     • normalize_phosphorylation_for_gromacs(pdb_file, output_file, copy_to_protein, force_field, phospho_ionic_state, user_text): Map phosphorylated residues for GROMACS pdb2gmx.
     • remodel_structure(target_pdb, donor_pdb, output_file, target_chain, donor_chain, mode, donor_residue_range, copy_missing_residues, copy_missing_atoms): Remodel experimental PDB by copying missing residues/atoms from a model structure.
     • separate_complex_components(pdb_file, output_dir, protein_output, ligand_output, ion_output): Automatically detect and separate all components (protein, ligands, ions) from a complex PDB file.
     • validate_structure(pdb_file, check_domain): Validate PDB file structure and integrity.
     • list_dir(directory_path): List files under the campaign or simulation root. Sandboxed — cannot leave the campaign tree.
     • grep_file(regex_pattern, filepath): Regex search in one file or the sandbox tree. Use to find pocket_mapped.json, MDP settings, or log errors.
     • read_inventory(stage): Read {stage}/inventory.json (absolute traj/topo, pocket_mapped, global_mapped). Prefer this over walking parent folders.

   **SIMSETUP AGENT:**
   Role: Topology, solvation, ions, MDP/TPR generation
     • build_simulation_system(protein_file, output_dir, ligand_file, ion_file, ligand_resname, ligand_itp, ion_resname, force_field, water_model, box_type, box_distance, ion_concentration, production_ns, temperature, pressure, extended_minimization): Build complete GROMACS simulation system from component PDB or GRO files.
     • convert_amber_to_gromacs(prmtop_file, inpcrd_file, output_top, output_gro): Convert AMBER prmtop/inpcrd files to GROMACS top/gro format.
     • generate_ligand_parameters(ligand_pdb, output_dir, charge_method, net_charge, atom_type, preferred_tool): Generate missing ligand topology parameters using acpype or antechamber.
     • map_ligand_atom_names(input_pdb, output_pdb, mapping_file, ligand_resname): Map ligand atom names from AlphaFold3/PDB format to AMBER force field format.
     • list_dir(directory_path): List files under the campaign or simulation root. Sandboxed — cannot leave the campaign tree.
     • grep_file(regex_pattern, filepath): Regex search in one file or the sandbox tree. Use to find pocket_mapped.json, MDP settings, or log errors.
     • read_inventory(stage): Read {stage}/inventory.json (absolute traj/topo, pocket_mapped, global_mapped). Prefer this over walking parent folders.

